# Third-party components

The firmware links or embeds the following. All are redistributable under
permissive terms, with one exception noted at the end.

| Component | Licence |
|---|---|
| ESP-IDF (Espressif) | Apache-2.0 |
| LVGL | MIT |
| TinyUSB (via `espressif/esp_tinyusb`) | MIT |
| Mbed TLS | Apache-2.0 |
| lwIP | BSD-3-Clause |
| FreeRTOS | MIT |
| `espressif/esp_lcd_sh8601` | Apache-2.0 |
| `espressif/esp_lcd_touch_cst816s` | Apache-2.0 |
| `espressif/esp_lvgl_port` | Apache-2.0 |
| `espressif/esp_websocket_client` | Apache-2.0 |
| `espressif/mdns` | Apache-2.0 |

MIT and BSD-3-Clause both require their copyright notice and licence text to
accompany binary distributions. Shipping a device means shipping those notices
somewhere the buyer can reach them -- the manual, a legal-notices page, or this
file in the source repository the device points at.

## The display initialisation table

`components/panel/sh8601_init_cmds.c` is 185 register writes copied verbatim
from Waveshare's `08_LVGL_Test` demo for the ESP32-S3-Knob-Touch-LCD-1.8.

Waveshare confirmed on enquiry (2026-09-27) that their demo code for ESP32
boards is released under **Apache-2.0** — MIT for their non-ESP hardware —
except where a particular part is bound by a third party's terms. That matches
this project's own licence, so it redistributes cleanly in source and in
binaries.

That confirmation came by correspondence rather than from a LICENSE file in
the demo package. Worth keeping the reply on file alongside the commercial
paperwork.

| Component | Licence |
|---|---|
| Waveshare ESP32-S3-Knob-Touch-LCD-1.8 demo (display init table) | Apache-2.0 |
